<title>JAPAN: Japan June gold imports down 35.1 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan June gold imports down 35.1 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in June fell by 35.1 percent from a year earlier to 11.33 tonnes, Ministry of Finance (MOF) data released on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>The figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  June 97   May 97    June 96</p>
<p> Total		  11.33     9.59	  17.45</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> South Africa	  2.06     3.60	   1.72</p>
<p> South Korea	   0.80     2.30	   2.60</p>
<p> Australia	     3.10     2.05	   4.05</p>
<p> Switzerland	   1.35     1.09	   2.60</p>
<p>Cumulative gold imports in the first six months of 1997</p>
<p>totalled 70.93 tonnes, down from 83.58 tonnes in the same</p>
<p>period a year earlier.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431</p>
</text>
